# Normalise text files; let each platform check out its native line endings by default.
* text=auto

# Files that run or are parsed inside the Linux container must stay LF whatever the local
# core.autocrlf says: a CRLF shebang makes s6 exec "bashio\r" and the add-on crash-loops
# (cost Argus a release). The Dockerfile strips CR defensively as well.
*.sh text eol=lf
switchboard/rootfs/** text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

*.png binary
